// The resources of nkb.exe, as a script for `build.rs` to compile: the
// program's icon, and the file's details - version, author, licence. Nothing
// else goes in, no manifest, the same two things nkb-gui.exe carries.
//
// The command line tool has no window, but its file is still seen: in the
// file manager, in a terminal's tab and in the task manager. It wears the
// palette's icon so the two files read as one product.
//
// The details are written at build time from the package manifest, by
// file_details.rs, into the build's output directory, which the build script
// hands the compiler as a place to look for includes. The code page is named
// here, before the include, because the compiler honours it only in the
// script it was asked to compile - crates/nkb-gui/assets/nkb-gui.rc says how
// that was found.
#pragma code_page(65001)
#include "details.rc"

// The path is relative to this file. ONE icon file for both programs, kept with
// the drawings it is made from and the tests that hold it to them - a copy here
// would drift. Only the build reads it, so nkb links nothing of the interface.
1 ICON "../../nkb-gui/assets/edamame.ico"
